<PracticeSet />

<AtTheTable>

Fractional Kelly is a sensitivity choice under estimation error, not a guarantee against drawdowns. Keep model-based sizing separate from the fixed-unit ruin model.

<FinalLinks />

</AtTheTable>

<QuantCorner>

Position sizing controls the sequence of wealth multipliers, not just the next trade’s mean profit. Forecast uncertainty and correlated exposures can invalidate a single-opportunity Kelly calculation.

</QuantCorner>
